{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381165-v20-assamite-sorcerer-rituals","id":1381165,"title":"V20 - Assamite Sorcerer Rituals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-13T18:27:47-07:00","id":1381165,"title":"V20 - Assamite Sorcerer Rituals","content":"Question about two assamite rituals in the book V20 Tome of Secrets, pages 42 and 43:<br /> Strength of Haqim (level 1)<br /> Strength in Wisdom (level 3)<br /> First of all, i'd like to thank you all for all topics created here it really helped me to figure out a lot of things regarding this game.<br /> Here it goes, how does both of the rituals work?<br /> First one increases difficult to everything, including Willpower rolls?<br /> The second one states that if you make a 5 success roll you get 5 to each physical and another 5 for each mental atribute, wich means 30 points to split between these two atributes, even surpassing generational limits, wich can be easily countered with PoB 3? Seems way better than Abyss Mysticism buff.<br /> How would you guys deal with these two rituals, cuz I think they are pretty much insane for power gamers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25853-moloch-the-gate-keeper","name":"Moloch The Gate Keeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25853_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T02:45:44-07:00","id":1381247,"title":"","content":"The way I read it, both are purely defensive in nature.<br /> Strength of Haqim for example doesn't give you better Willpower, but your Willpower counts as though it was higher if someone tries to dominate you.<br /> Same with Strength in Wisdom: it only helps you in defending yourself. Protecting yourself from a grapple, tackle or seduction, sure. Decapitations or negotiations? Nope.<br /> <br /> One thing I'd add to both of these rituals is a time limit of some sort, so they're not permanent buffs. Also, make sure they don't stack xP","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Furthermore, I believe Carthage should be destroyed.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23835-pang4","name":"pang4","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T18:35:01-07:00","id":1382275,"title":"","content":"Thanks mate, facing some issues with power players here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25853-moloch-the-gate-keeper","name":"Moloch The Gate Keeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25853_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T23:30:18-07:00","id":1382454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pang4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381165-v20-assamite-sorcerer-rituals?p=1381247#post1381247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I read it, both are purely defensive in nature.<br /> Strength of Haqim for example doesn't give you better Willpower, but your Willpower counts as though it was higher if someone tries to dominate you.</div> </div> </div> </div> Would it count as if adding to your Auspex for the purposes of resisting Obfuscate or Chimerstry, or would it add to the dice pool for contesting it if Auspex and Obf/Chimer are equal?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T23:55:53-07:00","id":1382459,"title":"","content":"I'm not familiar with the rituals in question, but if I were the storyteller I <b>definitely</b> wouldn't be giving free temporary discipline dots to a character based on a low or medium level ritual that also has broader applications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}